message: "If you use this code or the analysis plan, please cite it as below."
title: "Where does active case finding for TB still pay in India? Code, data and pre-registered plans"
abstract: >-
  Code, data, outputs and two pre-registered analysis plans for a study of
  India's published active case-finding (ACF) figures for tuberculosis. The
  v1.0.0 audit checks whether the published ACF and TB Mukt Bharat Abhiyaan
  figures are internally and mutually consistent, whether differences in
  definition, window or cut-off date explain their disagreements, what
  State-level ACF yields are, and whether TB notifications rose more, against
  each State's own trend, in States with a larger share of districts in phase 1
  of the campaign. The v1.1.0 extension, registered separately, asks three
  policy questions of State-level data (observational associations, not
  causal estimates): whether diagnoses rise less than proportionally with
  screening volume within States, whether campaign screening was aimed at
  States with higher prior yield, and whether State notifications move with ACF
  diagnoses.
